      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There are several reasons why a single room may not be cooling properly, despite the AC system working correctly throughout the rest of the house. Some common causes include: \n\n1. Blocked or dirty air vents in the non-cooling room, HVAC system imbalance, \n2. Imbalanced or uneven temperature settings across different rooms,\n3. Incorrectly sized AC unit, \n4. Refrigerant leaks, issues with the condenser unit, or poor insulation,\n5. Drafts or windows that allow hot air to enter the room from outside, or poor window seals",
